# @<%= orgScope %>/fdc3-plugin

FDC3 3.0 for apps running under OneTerminal. It runs the official
[`@finos/fdc3-agent-proxy`](https://www.npmjs.com/package/@finos/fdc3-agent-proxy)
over a WebSocket to the Desktop Agent, speaking the standard Desktop Agent
Communication Protocol (DACP).

## Usage

Load `fdc3-plugin.js` as an ES module. Importing it connects to the Desktop Agent,
sets `window.fdc3` and fires the standard `fdc3Ready` event.

```html
<meta name="ot-fdc3-app-id" content="my-app-id" />
<script type="module">
  import { getAgent } from "/fdc3-plugin.js";

  const fdc3 = await getAgent();
  await fdc3.addContextListener("fdc3.instrument", (context, metadata) => {
    console.log(context, metadata.source);
  });
</script>
```

`getAgent()` rejects with `AgentNotFound` if the page can't connect; the reason is in
the error's `cause`. Apps that use the `@finos/fdc3` package can call its `getAgent()`
instead, which finds `window.fdc3`.

Apps get the full FDC3 3.0 `DesktopAgent` API. Use `getInfo().appMetadata` to read the
app's own identity.

Inside a Terminal, the Terminal owns the panel's user channel. `window.OT_FDC3_INITIAL_CHANNEL`
is defined (possibly `null`) there, so check for `undefined` before joining a default channel
when running standalone.

## App id

The first non-empty value wins:

1. `<meta name="ot-fdc3-app-id">`
2. The `fdc3AppId` query parameter
3. The document title

App ids are self-asserted: the Desktop Agent doesn't authenticate them.

## Bus URL

The first non-empty value wins:

1. `<meta name="ot-fdc3-bus-url">`
2. `window.OT_FDC3_AGENT_URL`, injected by the Terminal
3. `window.OT_FDC3_BUS_URL`
4. `ws://localhost:7891/fdc3`

An injected empty `OT_FDC3_AGENT_URL` means FDC3 is disabled for this Terminal, and
`getAgent()` rejects.

## Limitations

- `fdc3.close()` works only for windows the Desktop Agent opened. Terminal panels and
  apps on a separate engine host reject with `ErrorOnClose`.
- Agent Bridging isn't implemented: `getInfo().optionalFeatures.DesktopAgentBridging` is `false`.
- The connection doesn't reconnect if the Desktop Agent restarts. Reload the app.

## Developing

`fdc3-plugin.js` is generated from `src/` and committed, so that Rust's `include_str!`,
the sample servers and scaffolded workspaces can use it without a JS build.

```sh
npm run build:fdc3-plugin   # rebuild fdc3-plugin.js; CI fails if you forget
npm run test:fdc3-plugin    # contract tests: the real proxy against the real Rust bus
```

The contract tests validate every frame in both directions against the FDC3 3.0 JSON schemas.
